{%- comment -%}
The email address as a link, without ever writing it whole into the page.
The two halves go out reversed and with no "@", so a scraper reading the
source finds nothing shaped like an address; _js/email.js reassembles them
into a mailto link in the browser. Without JavaScript the link reads
"name (at) domain (dot) com" and goes nowhere.
{%- endcomment -%}
{%- assign email_user_reversed = site.email_user | split: "" | reverse | join: "" -%}
{%- assign email_domain_reversed = site.email_domain | split: "" | reverse | join: "" -%}
<a data-email-user="{{ email_user_reversed }}" data-email-domain="{{ email_domain_reversed }}">{{ site.email_user }} (at) {{ site.email_domain | replace: ".", " (dot) " }}</a>
